{"compatibility":"as-is","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: as-is.

Protected data: `y_calib`, `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

No changes were required. Both protected observations are top-level data variables and are each observed exactly once with a plain built-in sampling statement. The parameters `a`, `b`, and `sigma` each have exactly one built-in prior sampling statement before later use.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=1> N;  // Number of observations
  array[N] real y;       // Observations

  int<lower=1> N_calib;  // Number of calibration observations
  array[N_calib] real y_calib; // Calibration observations
}

parameters {
  real a;
  real b;
  real<lower=0> sigma;
}

model {
  // Prior model
  a ~ normal(0, 1);
  b ~ normal(0, 1);
  sigma ~ normal(0, 1);

  // Calibration observational model
  y_calib ~ normal(0, sigma);

  // Observational model
  y ~ normal(a + b, sigma);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"N":5,"N_calib":1,"y":[5.0,5.0,5.0,4.0,3.0],"y_calib":[1.0]}","protected_variables":["y_calib","y"]}
